WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.320
As a fat person

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.200
I get a lot of abuse.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.040
From example, from people in cars.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.920
People is just a nice word for men.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.960
It's not to be all like
#allmenaretrash,

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.680
it's just that it's never women
shouting from cars.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.720
It's just never "I like your fringe!"

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.360
Or, "Where did you get those glasses?
They really suit your face!"

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.160
It's like they have this idea that

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.360
fat people are so desperate
to get laid

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:40.120
that anytime a van blasting loud
music through open windows passes,

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.040
we're just like, "Oh my god...

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:44.240
maybe that’s the one."

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.720
Here's a public service announcement
on behalf of all fat people.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.800
We don't wanna (boing) you either.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:56.560
Most of us actually have some err...
(fog horn noise) at home.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.320
At the moment it seems as if
body positivity is the new thing.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.840
It's all over Instagram.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.720
Thin to maybe chubby

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:11.560
white feminine cis women showing
that actually, if they try real hard,

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.760
they can look a bit fat too.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.600
Don't get me wrong, society has
made it very clear that no-one

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:20.160
fat or thin should be happy
with their bodies.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.560
We're all struggling.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:25.720
But the people who are the most
oppressed in society

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.320
like actually fat people, black
people and people of colour,

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.440
queer people, trans people, Muslims,
people with disabilities

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:36.720
are not at all represented
in the body positivity movement.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.720
So here is what has happened,

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.720
and strap in because this
is excellent information.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.080
In 1967 as a lot of social movements
called for justice,

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.520
a "Fat-In" was staged at
Central Park in New York.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:55.680
500 fat people gathered to eat
ice cream and burn diet books,

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.440
which, FYI, I will now be doing every
Sunday in Hyde Park - join me.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:05.280
NAAFA, the National Association
to Advance Fat Acceptance

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:09.400
was founded in America
in 1969 by Bill Fabrey,

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.960
in response to discrimination
against his wife.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:16.120
#relationshipgoals
The next time someone is rude to you,

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.240
if your partner doesn’t start
a social movement...

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:22.400
#leavehim #boybye

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:27.720
In 1973, two people called Judy
Freespirit and Aldebaran wrote:

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.560
the Fat Liberation Manifesto

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.120
which called for fat people
to have equal rights.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.920
Declared that the diet industry was
the enemy and stated that they were

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:40.160
fully entitled to human respect
and recognition.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.720
There were a lot of points
in the manifesto

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.440
and none of them were

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:48.240
love your curves or
#yourbodyisbeautiful.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.640
Because it doesn’t matter
how much I love my curves,

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:56.720
I will still be discriminated
against on a daily basis

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.320
and have a harder time buying clothes

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.320
anywhere that doesn’t
have flowers on it.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:04.800
And I will still have men
shout at me from cars.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:09.520
Fat has been made into body,
to make it more palatable.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.240
And liberation has been
made into positivity,

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:17.320
to remove all accountability
from the perpetrators.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:23.200
Body positivity is just another way
of asking women to smile.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.720
Thankfully, women love
being asked to smile.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.120
Oh no wait, no wait umm...

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:32.000
women love having autonomy
over their own bodies.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.000
I always get those two confused.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:44.920
Thanks for watching. 
Don’t forget to subscribe! :)

